Date: Sun, 4 Oct 2026 04:53:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(subject): show character portraits from the top instead
 of a center crop

The `grid` image is a 100x100 square that the backend center-crops
(`/r/100x100/`). Character portraits are usually full-body, so the square
only shows the waist and legs, and the 3:4 cover then crops it again.

Use the `medium` image (width-limited, original aspect ratio) and crop it
from the top with CSS, matching the legacy site. Falls back to `grid`
when `medium` is missing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JUFGFXc68QQGjEYNk7Y9E1
Signed-off-by: laraliang1225 <smalllicheng@gmail.com>
